  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 and avgpool, reaching 0.650 validation accuracy and 0.628 F1, while multiprofile avgpool also clearly helped PCA. The key uncertainty is whether scvi_n200’s performance depends on multiprofile aggregation or would be competitive as a simpler single-profile model. config_004 tests single-profile scvi_n200, directly isolating the profile-setting effect for the most promising RNA encoder without introducing image or fusion variables. This exploits the best-known representation while reducing uncertainty about whether added multiprofile complexity is necessary, making it a high-information next experiment under a limited budget."
